; effects.xon -- the delve set's sounds for what the player does and
; what holds them: the messages a turn tells, the conditions they are
; under, and the bonuses their rings give (docs/sound.md).
;
; (said "KEY" "SOUND") is heard when a turn tells message KEY.  A key
; whose event has a cue of its own (a blow, gold, the stairs, hunger,
; the lamp) is left to the cue.
;
; (condition "NAME" PROP ...) and (bonus "NAME" PROP ...) shape what is
; heard while the player is under a condition or wears a ring of a
; bonus: (on "SOUND") as it begins, (off "SOUND") as it ends, (every
; "SOUND" EVERY-MS GAIN) heard now and again while it holds, and (steps
; CENTS WANDER PCT) the player's steps CENTS sharper, flatter below
; nought, heard as much as WANDER percent of the time a side off, at PCT
; percent.  A bonus has (struck "SOUND") with a blow that lands on the
; player, (strikes "SOUND") with one the player lands, and (mends
; "SOUND") with hit points come back a little at a time.  A ring's
; bonus is heard whether its kind is known or not: it can be told by
; ear.

; --- the messages ---------------------------------------------------------------

(said "door" "door-creak")
(said "go-in" "door-creak")
(said "go-into" "door-creak")
(said "go-out" "door-creak")
(said "found-secret" "stone-grind")
(said "found-trap" "trap-click")
(said "trapped" "trap-snap")
(said "teleported" "blink")
(said "banished" "blink")
(said "mapped" "unfurl")
(said "ate" "munch")
(said "filled" "glug")
(said "put-on" "clink")
(said "took-off" "clink-off")
(said "removed" "clink-off")
(said "wielding" "draw")
